Let word be "226".
Let size be the number of characters in word.
Let ways be a list of size plus 1 zeros.
Set item 0 of ways to 1.
For every position from 1 to size.
Let previous be one less than position.
Let first digit be character previous of word minus 48.
If first digit is more than 0, set item position of ways to item previous of ways.
Let second digit be 0.
If position is more than 1, set second digit to character (position minus 2) of word minus 48.
Let pair be second digit times 10 plus first digit.
If position is more than 1 and pair is at least 10 and pair is at most 26, set item position of ways to item position of ways plus item (position minus 2) of ways.

Print item size of ways.
